 -- Aegis Developers <dev@aegis-os.org>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:05:00 +0000

aegis-shell (1.7.0-m4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * SettingsApp: `property bool recoverySeen` was declared on the aegisIdPane
    Component itself — "Component objects cannot declare new properties"
    (SettingsApp.qml:316). This is the error that survived the v0.6.10 and
    v0.6.11 rounds: Qt reports whole-document compile failures one at a time,
    so each fix revealed the next (v0.6.9 grouped `font {};`, v0.6.10
    font.color, v0.6.11 this one). The property moves into the idPane
    ColumnLayout; the recovery-key card logic is unchanged.
  * New guard: scripts/qml-guard.py runs the three known killer classes
    (grouped-property-with-semicolon, invalid font sub-properties,
    Component-scope properties) over every shell QML file, plus brace/
    duplicate-id/stray-token checks — a pre-tag step in VERIFY.md.
  * boot-capture: the app diag now also prints SETTINGS-ERR and runs a
    foreground QML probe (landed in v0.6.11 but worth the reminder: the
    v0.6.11 errorString was captured this way, straight from the guest).

 -- Aegis Developers <dev@aegis-os.org>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:35:00 +0000

aegis-shell (1.7.0-m3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * SettingsApp: Text used a non-existent grouped sub-property (font.color)
    in the Network pane — QFont has no color member, and Qt 6 compiles the
    whole document including deferred panes, so a single unknown property
    failed the entire Settings load (aegis-apps exit 1, no window ever
    mapped; v0.6.10 boot test, diff-vs-home 3.0 on both attempts). The Text
    color moves to the Text-level `color:` property.
  * SettingsApp: add the missing `import Aegis.Files` — the wallpaper image
    picker resolves Files.pathOf / Files.homeUrl().
  * Wrappers: aegis-settings / aegis-files now forward "$@" so
    `aegis-settings 8` really opens pane 8 (Aegis ID) — the argument was
    silently dropped before.
  * boot-capture: the pane-8 launch keeps stderr on the guest at
    /tmp/aegis-settings.err and the post-capture diag prints it, plus a
    foreground `timeout 6 aegis-apps settings 8` probe — a QML load failure
    can no longer reach the release without its errorString in the log.

 -- Aegis Developers <dev@aegis-os.org>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +0000

aegis-shell (1.7.0-m2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * SettingsApp: 12 grouped `font { ... }` blocks sat on the same line as
    `;`-separated bindings — this Qt's parser rejects the semicolon next to
    a grouped property ("Unexpected token ';'", four surfaces at a time).
    All converted to the shipped dotted form (font.pixelSize / font.bold).
  * FilesApp: FolderListModel has no showDotAndHidden in Qt 6 — the property
    is showHidden (docs: showDotAndDotDot covers ./.. only). The Show-hidden
    toggle bound a non-existent property and blocked the whole app load.
  * SettingsApp: the §6 panes array moves to the Window (win.panes) — it was
    declared on the inner AppWindow item, a lookup that the boot tests never
    exposed because the QML errors above kept both apps from opening since
    they landed.

